infographic sequence-snake-steps-underline-text
data
  title Health-check lifecycle: how a backend leaves and re-enters the pool
  desc Detection is not instant — it costs whole probe intervals
  sequences
    - label Healthy & serving traffic
      desc Probed every 10-30 s on a fixed interval
    - label 2-3 consecutive probes fail
      desc Crash detected within one to a few intervals
    - label Marked unhealthy, removed from pool
      desc New requests stop routing here; in-flight ones complete or time out
    - label Backend recovers, probes start passing
      desc Still excluded until it proves stable
    - label 2-3 consecutive successes
      desc Re-added to the pool, traffic redistributes
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f43f5e #14b8a6
